<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- Quantum HTML + CSS example 19_custom_properties/14: Theme toggle with :has() -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Theme toggle with :has()</title>
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: #1f2933;
      background: #f5f7fa;
    }
    .demo { max-width: 60rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem; }
    .demo > h1 { margin: 0 0 0.25rem; font-size: 2rem; }
    .lead { margin: 0 0 2rem; color: #52606d; }

    :root { --bg: #f8fafc; --fg: #0f172a; --card: #fff; }
    :root:has(#dark:checked) { --bg: #0f172a; --fg: #e2e8f0; --card: #1e293b; }
    body { background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg); transition: background-color 0.3s, color 0.3s; }
    .card { background: var(--card); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 14px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="demo">
    <h1>Theme toggle with :has()</h1>
    <p class="lead">A checkbox flips the variables for the whole page.</p>
    <label><input type="checkbox" id="dark"> Dark theme</label>
    <article class="card"><h2>Toggled by CSS</h2><p>No JavaScript: :has() watches the checkbox.</p></article>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
